  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Drain the tuna well and flake it into a bowl with a fork, breaking up any big chunks."
    },
    {
      "text": "Dress it with the olive oil and lemon juice, folding as you go - good tuna needs less than you think."
    },
    {
      "text": "Fold in the celery and half the parsley, then season with the salt and pepper. Keep it chunky - this is a salad, not a paste."
    },
    {
      "text": "Taste and adjust: more lemon if it tastes flat, a pinch more salt if it tastes shy."
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast the bread until the edges are crisp and the centers still have a little give."
    },
    {
      "text": "Pile the tuna salad onto the toasts and finish with the rest of the parsley."
    },
    {
      "text": "To make ahead: chill the salad up to two days and toast the bread when serving; keep the two separate until the table."
    }
  ],
